= The Iranian Embassy Siege

Gunmen have held the Iranian Embassy in Princes Gate for six days. When they kill a hostage, you authorise the SAS to storm the building. On live television, soldiers abseil down the front of the embassy. Nineteen of the twenty hostages are freed.

The country is gripped, and the government looks decisive.
